kubelet: The Agent Between Master and Worker Nodes
The kubelet is the agent that runs on each worker node in a Kubernetes cluster. It communicates with the master node and ensures that the containers on its node are running and healthy.
The kubelet reports the status of the node and the pods back to the master node, which is crucial for maintaining the cluster's health and availability. The kubelet also implements liveness/readiness/startup probes, 
runs init containers in order, and handles volume mounting. If the kubelet dies, the node goes NotReady, and pods may be evicted. This ensures that the cluster remains operational and responsive to change


